  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Refund to World Vision for procurement of spare parts for Fleet and SDB projects</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD is presently managing a Fleet  of vehicles and motor bikes under the Fleet Management and Safe and Dignified Burial projects. in other to be donor compliance due to the amount of money involve and the processes and time this will take, CAFOD formally requested World Vision to place vehicle and motorbike spare parts on its behalf. 
a single bulk purchase order was made by World Vision to procure these parts using their identified preferred supplier. 

Invoices have been submitted by World Vision for this procurement and this project will reimburse World Vision&apos;s expenses.</narrative>
  </description>
